 "answer": "Ollama uses a **32k** context by default on a GPU with 32 GiB of VRAM. The context-length doc lists the defaults by VRAM tier, and the 24–48 GiB tier is: \"24-48 GiB VRAM: 32k context\" [ollama/docs/context-length.md].\n\nThe FAQ says \"By default, Ollama uses a context window size of 4096 tokens\" [ollama/docs/faq.md]. That conflicts with the VRAM-tiered figure. I'd rely on the context-length doc, since it's specific to VRAM tiers, but the FAQ may be out of date. You can override the default with `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH` or the `num_ctx` parameter [ollama/docs/faq.md].",
